  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The 8(a) Business Development set-aside program obligated $7.2B in FY2026 to date across 8,971 awards, with an average award size of $806K and obligations down 47.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $3.6B of the total. The top industries by obligations are Computer Systems Design Services at $882M, Other Computer Related Services at $745M, and Facilities Support Services at $712M. Top vendors include AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC at $91.8M and CHEROKEE NATION STRATEGIC PROGRAMS, L.L.C. at $81.4M. Fiscal-year trends show past totals of $11.3B in FY21, rising to $15.1B in FY24, then falling to $13.7B in FY25 and to $7.2B in FY26 to date. The average award size and award count indicate many mid-sized transactions. Contractors should note the concentration of buying in defense and professional services, and the program’s partial current-year total when comparing across fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are 8(a) obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads buying with $3.6B in obligations. The next largest buyers are the Department of Homeland Security at $637M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $618M. The top three industries together account for significant portions of the $7.2B total, with Computer Systems Design Services at $882M, Other Computer Related Services at $745M, and Facilities Support Services at $712M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What do top vendors and award metrics reveal for FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC is the largest vendor at $91.8M, followed by CHEROKEE NATION STRATEGIC PROGRAMS, L.L.C. at $81.4M and ASRC FEDERAL TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, LLC at $67.1M. The program delivered 8,971 awards with an average award size of $806K. Obligations are down 47.2% year over year, and FY26 to date totals are partial fiscal-year figures."
      }
    ]
  },
